<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600304/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600304/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600304/>;
    dc:modified '2023-01-23T15:12:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Correlation factor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A measure of the quality of the returned pulse from an altimeter or similar acoustic device. Correlation factor ranges from 0 to 1. A value of 1 represents a perfect return echo with negligible noise and distortion.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S06::S0600304'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600303/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600303/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600303/>;
    dc:modified '2023-01-23T15:12:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Energy level'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A measure of the intensity of echo return from an altimeter or similar acoustic device. Energy level ranges from 0 to 1 where 1 represents full saturation of the receiver. An energy level of 0.707 (square root of 2) is the theoretical perfect level as it represents the energy of a pure sine wave with an amplitude utilising the maximum dynamic range of the receiver.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S06::S0600303'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S06/current/S0600197/2/> .
